  "folder": "Stacks",
  "className": "LargestRectangleInHistogram",
  "statement": "Each value is the height of a bar of width one. Return the area of the largest rectangle that fits entirely inside the histogram.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= heights.Length <= 10^5",
    "0 <= heights[i] <= 10^4"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "Every maximal rectangle is capped by some bar being its full height. So for each bar, how far left and right can it extend before hitting something shorter?",
    "A monotonic increasing stack of indices answers that. While the incoming bar is shorter than the stack top, that top bar can extend no further right.",
    "On popping, the width runs from the new stack top (exclusive) to the current index (exclusive). A sentinel of height 0 at the end flushes the stack."
  ],
  "complexity": "O(n) time, O(n) space",
  "signature": "int Solve(int[] heights)",
